<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#copper">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Copper</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Copper is a reddish metal used since ancient times for tools, ornaments and, alloyed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a>, bronze. It was traded widely in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a> by states such as the Akkadian, Babylonian and Hittite empires. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> empires drew wealth from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copperbelt">Copperbelt</a>'s mines, while copper coinage was used in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s copper exports helped finance the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>.</p></div>
